%% sGLP's system code: the stochastic extension of GLP, defined in svGLP's
%% paper (sections/sglp.tex), outside the language and outside its catalogue.
%%
%% A program reaches this module only if it declares a population --- a kind
%% (`person <name>.`) or a run declaration --- and the linker then puts its
%% exports in the scope of every module of the program.  A program that
%% declares none cannot call person/2.
%%
%% person(T, X) is the entry point of the asking clause of a simulation
%% program (Definition "Simulation Program"): in place of the construct
%% process construct(T, X), the goal person(T, X) at agent a spawns p(X, S),
%% p the person procedure that a's stochastic person declares for the
%% interactive type T, and S the seed derived from the run's seed, a and the
%% identifier of the asked goal; and it registers X as an interactive variable
%% of a, whose assignments the run's log records (Definition "Interface
%% Variable, Log").  T is the constant whose name is the interactive type as
%% its person declaration writes it: 'Menu' for `Menu =::= p`, 'Menu?' for
%% `Menu? =::= p`.  X is the argument construct(T, X) is given: the reader of
%% the interactive variable where T is in writer mode, its writer where T is
%% in reader mode.
%%
%% person/2 is implemented by the runtime (glp_runtime/lib/sglp/person.dart)
%% and has no clauses.

exported procedure(X) person(Constant?, X).
